{{Elections in Kansas}}

The '''1992 United States Senate election in Kansas''' was held on November 3, 1992. Incumbent Republican Senator [[Bob Dole]] ran for re-election to a fifth term, defeating Gloria O'Dell, the Democratic nominee, in a landslide. Dole would ultimately not serve out his full six-year term, and resigned in 1996 to focus on his [[Bob Dole 1996 presidential campaign|unsuccessful presidential campaign]], triggering a [[1996 United States Senate special election in Kansas|special election]].

==Democratic primary==  
===Candidates===  
* Gloria O'Dell, special assistant to [[Kansas State Treasurer|State Treasurer]] [[Sally Thompson]], campaign operative<ref>{{cite news|title=Woman eyes campaign for Dole's Senate seat|newspaper=[[The Wichita Eagle]]|date=May 17, 1992|location=[[Wichita, Kansas]]|page=2B|url=https://www.newspapers.com/article/the-wichita-eagle/167243265/|access-date=March 4, 2025}}</ref>
* [[Fred Phelps]], [[Westboro Baptist Church]] founder, disbarred lawyer<ref>{{cite news|title=Phelps enters race for U.S. Senate seat|newspaper=[[The Wichita Eagle]]|date=June 11, 1992|location=[[Wichita, Kansas]]|page=3D|url=https://www.newspapers.com/article/the-wichita-eagle/167243374/|access-date=March 4, 2025}}</ref>

